**Honesty notes:**

- The IBM J. R&D POWER4 volume (Vol. 46, No. 1, 2002) very likely contained additional companion papers (verification, packaging), but I cannot confidently name their exact titles, so I have not included them.
- ISSCC papers (entries 5–10) tend to emphasize circuit techniques and final performance numbers more than the "problems hit and decisions made during closure" narrative that the exemplar POWER4 paper provides. They are in the genre but often at the shallower end of it.
- IBM J. R&D papers (entries 1–2, 11–12) tend to be the richest implementation retrospectives, closest to the Warnock et al. exemplar.
